00:30:05,910 --> 00:30:07,230
You can play with
that. We've ran

511
00:30:07,230 --> 00:30:08,985
through the example of nc,

512
00:30:08,985 --> 00:30:12,270
showed how it was
blocking things.

513
00:30:12,270 --> 00:30:17,535
But you do some
socat on your own.

514
00:30:17,535 --> 00:30:20,680
Try different ports
and things like that,

515
00:30:20,680 --> 00:30:24,710
like we did and be sure
to run Terraform destroy.

516
00:30:24,710 --> 00:30:27,285
You don't want to be charged
for all these resources.

517
00:30:27,285 --> 00:30:30,570
Let me say terraform destroy,

518
00:30:30,570 --> 00:30:33,405
and we will be good to go.

519
00:30:33,405 --> 00:30:36,240
Another thing you're going
to want to play with

520
00:30:36,240 --> 00:30:41,035
is maybe in the console,

521
00:30:41,035 --> 00:30:43,290
you want to change something up

522
00:30:43,290 --> 00:30:45,895
a little bit and then
re-run Terraform apply,

523
00:30:45,895 --> 00:30:47,575
and see what happens.

524
00:30:47,575 --> 00:30:49,570
See that it's
detected, like, hey,

525
00:30:49,570 --> 00:30:53,970
you added or changed
this firewall rule,

526
00:30:53,970 --> 00:30:55,670
and so I'm going to get it

527
00:30:55,670 --> 00:30:58,195
back to what I expect it to be.

528
00:30:58,195 --> 00:31:02,240
When I say I, Terraform
is saying that.

529
00:31:02,330 --> 00:31:09,620
With that, that ends our lesson
on creating a VPC in GCP,

530
00:31:09,620 --> 00:31:11,580
doing it through the console,

531
00:31:11,580 --> 00:31:15,515
and then doing it
through Terraform.

532
00:31:15,515 --> 00:31:24,310
Thanks.